{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"docker.io/curlimages/curl","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:03:15.427Z","source":{"name":"Docker Hub","api":"https://hub.docker.com/v2/repositories/curlimages/curl/","page":"https://hub.docker.com/r/curlimages/curl"},"readme":"# Official curl docker images\nThese are the official curl images generated by the curl docker team (curl-docker at haxx.se) or contact Jim Fuller (jim at webcomposite.com)\n\nLatest image is also available from [quay.io](https://quay.io/repository/curl/curl).\n\n# Latest tags and respective Dockerfile links\n\n* [8.21.0 (latest)](https://github.com/curl/curl-container/releases/tag/8.21.0) - bump curl 8.21.0 and bump alpine 3.24.1\n\n# Quick reference\n* Where to get help: [website](https://curl.se/), [mailing lists](https://curl.se/mail/), [Everything Curl](https://curl.se/book.html)\n* github repo: [curl/curl-docker](https://github.com/curl/curl-container)\n* Where to file issues: https://github.com/curl/curl-container/issues\n* Maintained by: The curl docker team (curl-container at curl.se) \n* License(s) - [license](https://curl.se/docs/copyright.html), check 3rd party documentation for license information\n\n\n# What is Curl ?\n[curl](https://curl.se/) is a command line tool and library  for transferring data with URLs.\n\n[curl](https://curl.se/)  is used in command lines or scripts to transfer data. It is also used in cars, television sets, routers, printers, audio equipment, mobile phones, tablets, settop boxes, media players and is the internet transfer backbone for thousands of software applications affecting billions of humans daily.\n\nSupports the following protocols (so far!):.\n\nDICT, FILE, FTP, FTPS, Gopher, HTTP, HTTPS, IMAP, IMAPS, LDAP, LDAPS, POP3, POP3S, RTMP, RTSP, SCP, SFTP, SMB, SMBS, SMTP, SMTPS, Telnet and TFTP. curl supports SSL certificates, HTTP POST, HTTP PUT, FTP uploading, HTTP form based upload, proxies, HTTP/2, cookies, user+password authentication (Basic, Plain, Digest, CRAM-MD5, NTLM, Negotiate and Kerberos), file transfer resume, proxy tunnelling and more.\n\n# How to use this image\n\n### getting docker image\nTo pull the latest version:\n```\n> docker pull curlimages/curl:8.21.0\n```\n\n### run docker image\nCheck everything works properly by running:\n```\n> docker run --rm curlimages/curl:8.21.0 --version\n```\nHere is a more specific example of running curl docker container: \n```\n> docker run --rm curlimages/curl:8.21.0 -L -v https://curl.se \n```\nTo work with files it is best to mount directory:\n```\n>  docker run --rm -it -v \"$PWD:/work\" curlimages/curl:8.21.0 -d@/work/test.txt https://httpbin.org/post\n```\n\nLooking for a base image to use ? go over to [curl-base](https://hub.docker.com/repository/docker/curlimages/curl/general).\n\n# Build\nThis version of curl built with the following configure options\n```\n--enable-static --disable-ldap --enable-ipv6 --enable-unix-sockets --with-ssl --with-libssh2 --with-nghttp2=/usr \\\n--prefix=/usr/local --with-gssapi\n```\nsupporting:\n```\nProtocols: dict file ftp ftps gopher gophers http https imap imaps mqtt pop3 pop3s rtsp scp sftp smb smbs smtp smtps telnet tftp\nFeatures: alt-svc AsynchDNS brotli HTTP2 HTTPS-proxy IPv6 Largefile libz NTLM NTLM_WB SSL TLS-SRP UnixSockets\n```\n\n# How to verify image\n\nImages are signed using [sigstore](https://www.sigstore.dev/). To view signatures of the image:\n\n```\ncosign tree curlimages/curl:8.21.0\n```\nImages are signed with cosign and can be verified with this public key:\n\n```\n-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----\nMFkwEwYHKoZIzj0CAQYIKoZIzj0DAQcDQgAEwFTRXl79xRiAFa5ZX4aZ7Vkdqmji\n5WY0zqc3bd6B08CsNftlYsu2gAqdWm0IlzoQpi2Zi5C437RTg/DgLQ6Bkg==\n-----END PUBLIC KEY-----\n```\nSave this to a file (ex. cosign.pub) and verify with cosign as follows:\n\n```\ncosign verify --key cosign.pub curlimages/curl:8.21.0\n```","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"curlimages","url":"https://hub.docker.com/u/curlimages","official":false,"verified":false},"registered":"2019-08-26T08:51:34.461815Z","updated":"2026-09-02T10:31:25.411729Z","categories":["Networking","Security","Integration & delivery"],"keywords":[],"license":null,"links":[],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":6702719476,"stars":209},"mediaTypes":["application/vnd.docker.container.image.v1+json","application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","application/vnd.oci.image.config.v1+json","application/vnd.oci.image.index.v1+json"],"contentTypes":["image"],"storage":2529160631,"tags":[{"name":"latest","digest":"sha256:58adaa4e8dca9c988bae2aba4ab3434a0bb2da16bbe3f92dec39ec7785166777","pushed":"2026-09-02T10:31:01.285687Z","size":10906041,"platforms":["linux/amd64","linux/ppc64le","linux/386","linux/arm/v7","linux/arm64/v8"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":"active"},{"name":"8.22.0","digest":"sha256:58adaa4e8dca9c988bae2aba4ab3434a0bb2da16bbe3f92dec39ec7785166777","pushed":"2026-09-02T10:30:56.629625Z","size":10906041,"platforms":["linux/amd64","linux/ppc64le","linux/386","linux/arm/v7","linux/arm64/v8"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":"active"},{"name":"8.21.0","digest":"sha256:7c12af72ceb38b7432ab85e1a265cff6ae58e06f95539d539b654f2cfa64bb13","pushed":"2026-06-24T09:30:14.695103Z","size":10835421,"platforms":["linux/amd64","linux/ppc64le","linux/386","linux/arm/v7","linux/arm64/v8"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":"active"},{"name":"8.20.0","digest":"sha256:b3f1fb2a51d923260350d21b8654bbc607164a987e2f7c84a0ac199a67df812a","pushed":"2026-04-29T10:11:28.668155Z","size":10805298,"platforms":["linux/amd64","linux/ppc64le","linux/386","linux/arm/v7","linux/arm64/v8"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":"active"},{"name":"8.19.0","digest":"sha256:c03110c736db81bbe1be0296f1f1608c81b954b01626bdfb0a8f84e5bd00ff3c","pushed":"2026-04-22T19:49:25.759837Z","size":1076